DELIVERABLE 10 -- THE RIDER: VERNIER-28's C20 CELL, RNG-MATCHED
============================================================================================================
  C20 = gamma 0.87 + 10 seeds, K_available ~ 19, ladder R1. Replayed with
  V28's own seeds: array W.make_array(2500 + r), universe seed 28000+977r+26,
  noise seed 880000+7919r+202, certification rng 880000+7919r+202+610000+1009.

  CONFIGURATION FACTS, BY INSPECTION, BEFORE ANY RUN:
    C20's priors are UNIFORM 10 pc for every pulsar (vernier28_lib.PRIOR_PC = vernier24.PRIOR_PC).
    Its array is V24 SYNTHETIC (isotropic directions, log-normal weights,
    log-uniform 0.3-5 kpc distances). There is no J0437, no sub-lambda anchor,
    and no heterogeneous prior of any kind.
    ==> H1 (sub-fringe priors trivialise) and H3 (scramble too small to
        displace) are DEAD FOR C20 BY CONSTRUCTION: every window is +-30 pc,
        the scramble is U(-500, 500) pc, and no pulsar is anywhere near a
        sub-fringe prior. Whatever opened C20 is not a real-prior mechanism.

  12 realisations, 121 certification steps, 5.9 combs per step (COMB_CAP = 16).
  exposure = 14036 pulsar-certifications
  SIGNAL certs 36 (of which true 36); SCRAMBLED-null certs 6
  null FPR = 0.043 %  95 % CI [0.016, 0.093] %
  null/signal ratio = 0.167   (V28's banked C20-R1 row: scrambled cert 0.50 per run on 1.42 phantom/run)

  STEP 1 -- per-pulsar leak table
    6 distinct pulsars fire in the null across all 121 steps; 17 fire on signal.
     pulsar idx  null fires  sig fires       K_i       w
              5           1          0     174.3    0.78
             27           1          0     175.6    0.57
             53           1          0     173.0    0.44
             67           1          0     167.5    1.71
             73           1          4     177.0    1.38
             90           1          0     166.7    0.15
    median K_i of null-firing pulsars = 173.6 vs 170.8 for the rest
    K_i range across the array = 146 - 192 (UNIFORM 10 pc priors -- the spread is pure geometry, dL = c/(f(1-cos mu)))
    pulsars at K_i <= 3 (the Anchor-Census sub-fringe class): 0  <-- H1 has nothing to bite on

  STEP 2 -- null-validity audit
    median scramble displacement = 714 fringes (range 607 - 798); pulsars below 3 fringes: 0
    window is +-30 pc, scramble is U(-500, 500) pc, so per comb P(displaced INTO the window) = 0.060
    with 5.9 combs per step, P(at least one comb in window) = 0.304
    ==> metric A (fringes) says the control is VALID; metric B (in-window)
        says a comb lands back inside the searched window in a sizeable
        minority of steps, and that probability GROWS with comb count.

  STEP 3 -- floor recut
      n_null  sig certs  null certs  null FPR %
          32          9           1       0.020
         128          6           0       0.000
    ==> H4 dead for C20 too: the floor is recut inside every `certify` call
        and quadrupling the nulls does not close it.

